1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maximilian_von_Alopaeus '''Magnus Maximilian von Alopaeus'''] was a Finnish diplomat. He was born in Viipuri and educated in Turku, later on Göttingen. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ''He first wanted'' to pursue for the ecclesiastical profession, but his employment as secretary by Count Nikita Ivanovich Panin, Russian ambassador at the Swedish court, was the first step in a gradual rise through the political 
2 CONC ranks.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1783, Alopeus''' was appointed resident-minister at the court of the Bishop of Lübeck, where he maintained the correspondence between Tsesarevich Paul and Frederick II. In 1789, Alopeus was sent to Berlin where he stayed for
2 CONC  6 years, gained favor from Frederick William II, and secured the signing of the allied treaty between Russia and Prussia. He was named minister plenipotentiary at the court of Berlin, by the Empress Catherine, in 1790.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1795, Prussia''' having withdrawn from the coalition by the Treaty of Basel, he remonstrated; and in 1796, he left Berlin, to which court he did not return till 1802. In 1802, he was appointed envoy at the Prussian court. Th
2 CONC e rapprochement of Russia and Prussia in 1806 to a considerable degree is due to his work. In 1807, he was sent to London as an ambassador, but the peace of Tilsit put his mission to an end.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alopeus participated in''' the Congress of Aix-la-Chapelle. He retired from diplomacy in 1820, to Frankfort-am-Main, where he lived till his death. He is said to have left very valuable manuscript memoirs.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''He was followed'' on his diplomatic career by his younger brother David Alopaeus.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''His daughter Natalie'' (ca.1796–1823) was married with Konstantin von Benckendorff.
2 CONT
2 CONT /////
2 CONT
2 CONT Osmo Durchman; Finska anor inom furstehus. Genos 5(1934), s. 37-87 
2 CONT
2 CONT Magnus (Maximilian) von (kurländskt indigenat 28. 2. 1784 nr. 220) Alopaeus, rysk envoyé, verkligt geheimeråd, döpt i Viborg 11.1.1748, d. i Frankfurt a. M. 6. 6. 1822.  - G. 1:o 1794 m. Johanna Hedvig Sophie Luise von Quast, f. 1
2 CONC 765, d. 179(6), dotter till godsägaren Johann Adolf Friedrich von Quast och Johanna Elisabeth von Diest; g.  - G. 2:o på Destedt vid Braunschweig 11.4.1799 m. Luise Charlotte Auguste von Veltheim, f. på Destedt 22.9.1768, d. i Bra
2 CONC unschweig 31.10.1851, dotter till överkammarherren hos hertigen av Braunschweig Johann Friedrich von Veltheim och hans 2:a hustru Margaretha Dorothea Sidonie von Münchhausen.
2 CONT
2 CONT etc. 
