1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Alopaeus '''Count Frans David Alopaeus'''] (sometimes also ''Alopeus'', ''von Alopaeus'' or ''Alopäeus'') (December 19, 1769 in Vyborg – June 13, 1831 in Berlin) was an Finnish 
2 CONC Imperial Russian diplomat. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He followed his''' older brother Maximilian von Alopaeus into a diplomatic career. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He was enrolled''' at the Military Academy in Stuttgart from 1781 to 1785. He studied at the Georg-August-Universität in Göttingen. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He was the''' Imperial Russian ambassador to Stockholm from 1803, and took part in the negotiations for the Peace of Hamina Treaty in 1809. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''After the Treaty''' of Hamina his next diplomatic success involved Russo-Turkish relationships. When Napoleon started his campaign against Russia, with Turkey not joining the campaign, has been widely perceived due to the effor
2 CONC ts of Alopaeus. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Later in his''' career he participated in arranging the marriage between Grand Duke Nikolay Pavlovich, later Tsar Nicholas I and Charlotte, the daughter of the King of Prussia Wilhelm III. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He was granted''' a first a title of a Baron in Finland, then one of a Count along with the coat of arms in 1820 in Poland by the  Congress of Poland for his successful negotiations on Poland's borders with the Kingdom of Pruss
2 CONC ia.
