1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Joachim Zachris Duncker=
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joachim_Zachris_Duncker '''Joachim Zachris Duncker'''] was a Swedish soldier born in [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ristiina Ristiina] in the Province of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Savonia_(histo
2 CONC rical_province Savonia].
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1789 Duncker obtained''' the rank of 2nd Lieutenant in the Savonian ranger regiment. He first fought in the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russo-Swedish_War_(1788%E2%80%931790 Russo-Swedish war of 1788-1790], and proved his 
2 CONC valor at the Battle of Perttimäki. In 1804 Duncker was promoted to Captain.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''During the''' [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Finnish_War Finnish War of 1808-1809] he distinguished himself as a brave and prominent officer. When [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johan_Adam_Cronstedt Cronstedt]'s army had to ret
2 CONC reat nortbound from Savonia, via Mikkeli, via Kuopio to Iisalmi and towards Oulu in the Northern Oshtrobothnia region, Duncker commanded the army's rearguard. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''During the''' [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Pulkkila Battle of Pulkkila] (2 May 1808) he distinguished himself so well that [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johan_August_Sandels Johan August Sandels] gave him the honor
2 CONC ary assignment to bring the news of the victory to the King of Sweden. Shortly after, he was promoted to Major. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In June 1808 he''' captured a large transport of supplies to the Russians. During the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Koljonvirta Battle of Koljonvirta] (27 October 1808), Duncker together with Colonel Fahlander and [h
2 CONC ttps://www.geni.com/people/Lt-Col-Carl-Wilhelm-Malm/6000000002908252082 Major Malm] and only 600 men helped Sandels to utterly defeated a superior Russian force. In 1809 Duncker fought the Russians in the Swedish province of Väste
2 CONC rbotten, and was promoted to Lieutenant-Colonel. During the Battle of Hörnefors (5 July 1809) Duncker commanded the Swedish rearguard and received fatal wounds and died in the Russian encampment the day after.
2 CONT
2 CONT Duncker was buried next to Umeå church by the Russians that gave him a full honour guard. He lies buried together with a Russian cossack chief. In 1897 a memorial was erected on the spot where the grave was assumed to be.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joachim_Zachris_Duncker?wprov=sfla1
