2 CONT https://www.jordans.org/SavonAsukkaat/ps12/ps12_089.html
2 CONT
2 CONT In the in the History of Savo (Kauko Pirinen: Savon historia II:1,
2 CONT Kustannuskiila Oy, Pieksamäki 1982, p.214)I found something very
2 CONT interesting for you. Pirinen mentions that a cavalryman Sigfrid
2 CONT Pentinpoika was in 17th century a leaseholder of the farm Kasanen in
2 CONT Kerisalo, and used name Ruth. Pirinen also says that the Kerisalo-farm
2 CONT remained thereafter in the hands of the descendants of Sigfrid. Why did
2 CONT Sigfrid use the name Ruth (Ruuth) I do not know. There are several
2 CONT Ruuth-families in Finland. One of them lived in 16th century in Viipuri
2 CONT and was very rich. The Ruuths in eastern Finland might be their
2 CONT descendants, but as you said Ruth might be a soldier name too.
2 CONT
2 CONT the above material from:Jouko Salminen
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigfried Bengtsson should be the first then...
2 CONT but there are no Bengt Ruuts, Sigfried Ruuts.
2 CONT there are no Sipiläs before about 1750
